Me:
what gradio output components should i use for each tab of my finance assistant and why

AI:
For the spending analysis tab use gr.Textbox with lines set to 30 so the full report fits without scrolling. For the chat tab use gr.Chatbot which displays messages as a two-column conversation like WhatsApp — user messages on the right, FinBot replies on the left — which is much more natural than a plain textbox that shows everything as flat text. For the RAG tips tab use gr.Textbox with lines set to 12. For the savings calculator tab use gr.Textbox with lines set to 16 to fit the formatted savings plan.

The chat tab specifically needs gr.Chatbot and not gr.Textbox because gr.Chatbot automatically maintains and displays the full conversation history in the right format. If you used gr.Textbox for chat it would only show the last message.

Me: 
my csv has negative amounts like -$15.00 for xbox store refunds should i include them in the spending analysis or separate them

AI:
You should separate them. Including refunds in the category totals distorts the percentages and makes the report misleading. Here is what goes wrong if you include them:

Total = $69.99 + $60.00 + $17.00 + (-$15.00) = $131.99
Gaming percentage = 69.99 divided by 131.99 = 53.0 percent

That is inflated because the denominator is smaller than the real spending.

The correct approach is to calculate percentages using only positive spending, then show refunds as a separate line in the report:

Positive total = $69.99 + $60.00 + $17.00 = $146.99
Gaming percentage = 69.99 divided by 146.99 = 47.6 percent
Refunds shown separately: -$15.00 (Xbox Store Refund)

The percentages now sum correctly to 100 percent and the net spent figure shows the real money that left the account after refunds.

